----
id: phase1
title: Engagement opens
----

We announced the Los Angeles fires recovery topic on February 24, 2025.


----
id: phase2
title: Agenda setting
----

People affected by the Eaton and Palisades fires told us the issues that were most important to them. This shaped the community deliberations.


----
id: phase3
title: Review
linkTitle: See what we found in agenda setting
----

We reviewed the agenda-setting conversations. We examined the items that surfaced, analyzed data, and gathered insights. This helped us plan the deliberation phase. <a href="/lafires-recovery/agenda-setting-findings/">See what we found in agenda setting.</a>

----
id: phase4
title: Planning
----

The Engaged California team carefully set the stage for effective deliberation.

We used the takeaways from agenda setting to find the right policymakers to work with. We planned deliberations for both the Eaton and Palisades recovery areas.


----
id: phase5
title: Deliberation
----

Participants discussed what the community needed most. They reached consensus on how to get to a speedy and equitable recovery.

It was not easy. Some topics were triggering. But reaching consensus was important. It let survivors have a say in the actions they needed officials to take on fire recovery.


----
id: phase6
title: Reporting
----

We reviewed and analyzed the outcomes of the deliberation phase. We shared that report with government and community leaders. We worked with government officials to find actions survivors said they wanted. We posted a report of findings and actions. [See the action plan](/lafires-recovery/action-plan)

----
id: signup
----

Deliberations for LA fires recovery are happening now. Give us your email if you're interested in participating.
